  "statement_form": "SensitivityCampaign.AchievesExponent a: for every epsilon > 0 and every S >= 2 there is a total Boolean function f on Fin n bits with sensitivity(f) >= S and sensitivity(f)^(a-epsilon) <= blockSensitivity(f). Sensitivity is the largest number of single bit flips that change f, and block sensitivity is the largest number of disjoint nonempty bit sets that each change f at one input (Def_SensitivitySeparation, reviewed 2026-10-19). That is our statement: bs(f) >= s(f)^(alpha - o(1)) for a family of total Boolean functions with s(f) -> infinity.",
